 - `scene_palette`: Pick the colors run along strokes: `spectrum` (the prism rainbow), `moonlight` (white with a cool and warm shimmer), `gold`, `glacier`, `borealis`, `rose`, or None for the theme's own. In the prism looks it recolors every glowing curve and the lines the look runs a hue along; fringes, vignette and glow stay. One undo step.
 - `undo`: Revert the last edit (each patch, verb or narration is one step).
 - `redo`: Re-apply the edit that undo reverted.
-- `animate`: Animate with a choreography verb starting at a marker (or seconds). Timing comes from the theme. Returns when it starts and ends so the next step can follow it. `orbit` swings the 3D camera `value` degrees (default 360), until marker `until` if given; `morph` too runs until `until` if given. `transform` and `become` take `targets=[from, to]`; `sweep` takes `path` and `value`; `circumscribe` takes one target and `value` "circle" or "box".
+- `animate`: Animate with a choreography verb starting at a marker (or seconds). Timing comes from the theme. Returns when it starts and ends so the next step can follow it. `orbit` swings the 3D camera `value` degrees (default 360), until marker `until` if given; `lift` tips a flat 3D camera over to elevation `value` (default 32); `morph` too runs until `until` if given. `transform` and `become` take `targets=[from, to]`; `sweep` takes `path` and `value`; `circumscribe` takes one target and `value` "circle" or "box".
 - `narrate`: Set the narration. `[[name]]` puts a marker at the next word. Every animation anchored to a marker follows the voice. `pace` adds breathing room after busy sentences.
 - `checkpoint`: Remember the current document under `name` (to compare or return to later).
 - `restore`: Go back to a checkpoint, as one step (undo brings you back again).
